---
title: "agy acp channel session: one terminal post per person input"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Process
    lg1: Turn
    lg2: Session
    lg3: Breaks NoDuplicateExecution or NoReviveAfterClear in some cases
    lg4: Path to the NoDuplicateExecution or NoReviveAfterClear bug
  }
  class lg0 tan
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 teal
  class lg3 mayBreak
  class lg4 bugPath
  s0: No agy child
  s1: Child up, no session
  s2: Session idle
  s3: Input accepted, prompt not yet written
  s4: Prompt open
  s5: Turn steered: two prompts open
  s6: Turn answered, post pending
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s0: a person sends a message
  s0 --> s1: AgentDesk starts agy acp
  s1 --> s2: session/new
  s2 --> s3: actor claims and accepts the next input (new turn, or steer while a prompt is open)
  s3 --> s3: the input's origin is written ahead into the inflight row#59; its claim becomes an in-memory terminal
  s3 --> s4: session/prompt for the saved input (dropped as a failed steer if its turn is stopping)
  s4 --> s3: actor claims and accepts the next input (new turn, or steer while a prompt is open)
  s3 --> s5: session/prompt for the saved input (dropped as a failed steer if its turn is stopping)
  s5 --> s1: person runs /clear
  s5 --> s4: agy answers the prompt (stopReason)
  s1 --> s1: steer prompt fails#59; the input is put back in the queue
  s4 --> s6: steer prompt fails#59; the input is put back in the queue
  s6 --> s3: actor claims and accepts the next input (new turn, or steer while a prompt is open)
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
  class s0 tan
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 mayBreak
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 teal
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 blue
  class s4 mayBreak
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 blue
  class s5 bugPath
  class s6 teal
  class s6 bugPath
